Developers / explicit contracts One API. No fuzzy success. Start with the composed demo, inspect the OpenAPI surface, then use Python, TypeScript, or Go clients against explicit AIFENCE outcomes. Quickstart API reference Fastest proof Run the whole lifecycle. The demo creates an isolated tenant/key, submits through Quality → Guard → Bus, claims the handoff, and exits non-zero if completion is not truthful. $ aifence demo {
  "quality": {"passed": true},
  "guard": {"outcome": "allow"},
  "bus": {"delivered": true},
  "final_outcome": "handed_off"
} Python aifence-client with mTLS support and structured errors. TypeScript @aifence/client with bounded HTTP behavior. Go github.com/aifence/aifence-go and shared Bus TCK compatibility.
